  "name": "CHAOS Lab 2 · Wireglass (expressive lead)",
  "description": "A pitched, playable glass-and-wire lead: A's edged waveform interacts with B's near-sine via ring coupling; the comb adds metallic body, but the note remains musical. An ADSR drives stereo VCAs and also nudges coupling on note onset. Slow external LFOs shift coupling and the body's tuning; internal subtle pitch LFO adds vibrato. Echo is intentionally modest. CHAOS gate remains unpatched for real release. Expose: route, depth, shape_a, shape_b, detune, body_tune/mix, roughness/rate, internal lfo_rate/lfo_depth, ADSR attack/release and delay mix.",
